  "retitles": [
   {
    "code": "S2.012",
    "was": "Recognise and respond to linguistic devices, figurative language and imagery. twentieth and/or twenty-first centuries, including literature, fiction and non-fiction, and other forms of writing, such as discursive essays, reviews and articles. This study should include focus on writers\u2019 use of language and style and the ways in which writers achieve effects and influence readers. Candidates should study how influence may include fact, ideas, perspectives, opinions and bias.",
    "now": "Recognise and respond to linguistic devices, figurative language and imagery."
   },
   {
    "code": "S3.006",
    "was": "Demonstrate accuracy in spelling, punctuation and grammar. the ability to create and compose texts with a variety of forms and purposes, e.g. descriptive, narrative, discursive, argumentative and persuasive. This study should include focus on the following text types: letter, report, article, journal, speech, interview and summary.",
    "now": "Demonstrate accuracy in spelling, punctuation and grammar."
   },
   {
    "code": "S4.006",
    "was": "Engage appropriately in conversation. engaging conversations and to respond spontaneously to questions and prompts. This study should include focus on presentation skills in employing and organising content, and language devices, such as irony, tone and emphasis. write all their answers in the space provided on the question paper. should spend approximately 15 minutes reading the texts. explicit and implicit meanings. continuous writing of no more than 120 words. speech, interview and article. persuasive speech, letter or article. relevant year of assessment. completed in any order, and are: contribute to the final internally assessed mark or to the externally moderated mark for the portfolio. to moderate or standardise your teachers\u2019 marking so that all candidates are assessed to a common standard. (If only one teacher is marking internal assessments, no internal moderation is necessary.)",
    "now": "Engage appropriately in conversation."
   }
  ],
